unit: dm-rename-desktop-member
commits: ad62cfab1 (the renames)
what: sovereign-desktop's two Peer* type definitions renamed to their DT words,
  referrers repointed (the two doc comments in sovereign-turn-client's mesh.rs
  and sovereign-api's routes_internal/peer_preference.rs):
    DiscoveredPeerDto -> DiscoveredMemberDto
    PeerPreferenceDto -> VenuePreferenceDto
  PeerPreferenceDto is a `decided:merge` row: its target (the api's
  VenuePreferenceDto) still lives in sovereign-api, not
  sovereign-contracts::daemon_wire, and the desktop is a thin surface that may
  not reach sovereign-api (quality/ARCH_LAYERS.toml:1203, may_reach). So the
  row's "delete the desktop copy and use the api's" option is unavailable; the
  commit takes the other one — a serde-compatible struct (same four field
  names, no serde renames) renamed to the owner's word. The full merge waits on
  the promotion the DT row's own `why` names.
  The desktop's TypeScript mirror (src/lib/types.ts) is outside the campaign's
  Rust-only instrument and is untouched, as in the sibling rename rows.
checks: CLEAN exit=0 (disk gate; debug target 0G, cache kept); LINT exit=0
  (scoped to 7 crates incl. sovereign-desktop/-api/-turn-client); CENSUS
  --self-test exit=0 (11/11 positives caught, 11/11 negatives refused).
census: peer-outside 6 in 5 crates -> 4 in 4 crates (the desktop's two gone;
  the remaining four are the later rename rows' work).
